# MODIFIED. applyStyleEdit runs every edit through the guard first.

file: "packages/editor/src/state/create_editor_state.ts"
doc: "The reactive state for one editor session."

methods: [
  { name: "createEditorState"
    change_type: MODIFIED
    doc:
      "One change, inside the applyStyleEdit closure: the incoming edit is\n"
      "replaced by editableChanges(edit, getDiagram()) before anything else\n"
      "happens to it.\n"
      "\n"
      "It goes BEFORE the existing four-empty-lists early return, so an\n"
      "edit whose every change is dropped takes the same no-op path as an\n"
      "edit that arrived empty: no stylesheet write, no undo entry, no\n"
      "version bump, dirty unchanged.\n"
      "\n"
      "The snapshot, the coalescing key, the undo log and the redo reset\n"
      "all then operate on the filtered edit, so an undo restores exactly\n"
      "what was written.\n"
      "\n"
      "acceptPending is guarded too, at its applyStyleEditToStylesheet\n"
      "call: accepting a proposal about an element this diagram does not\n"
      "contain writes the same dead entry as editing one directly. A\n"
      "proposal whose every change is dropped is still REMOVED from\n"
      "pendingEdits -- it has been reviewed, and leaving it listed would\n"
      "make it unacceptable and unrejectable.\n"
      "\n"
      "appendPendingEdit is NOT guarded. A pending edit is a proposal\n"
      "stored in the stylesheet for someone else to accept later, and it\n"
      "is authored against a diagram this session may not be holding."
    output: { named: { symbol: "EditorState" } }
    uses: ["editableChanges"]
  }
]
